{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And you shall be holy men to Me</b> — The reason for this verse is that until now Scripture has mentioned the laws and warned concerning things that defile. And now, when it comes to begin with the prohibition of foods, it opens and says <b>and you shall be holy men to Me</b>, for it is fitting that a person should eat everything by which he lives, and the prohibitions in foods are nothing but purity of the soul, that you should eat clean things that do not produce coarseness and grossness in the soul. Therefore it says \"and you shall be holy men to Me,\" that is to say, I desire that you be holy men in order that you be worthy of cleaving to Me, for I am holy. Consequently, do not make your souls loathsome through eating abominable things. And thus it says (Leviticus 11:43–44): \"You shall not make your souls abominable through any swarming thing that swarms, and you shall not defile yourselves through them and be defiled through them, for I am YHWH your Elohim, and you shall sanctify yourselves and be holy, for I am holy.\" Now the swarming creatures make the soul abominable, but the torn animal (טְרֵפָה) contains no abomination; rather, in guarding against it there is holiness."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:14:29.607535038Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}